      "description": "Watch Kortrijk vs Antwerp highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 17, 2026. On August 17, 2026 , the Jupiler Pro League showcased a compelling tactical battle as Kortrijk hosted Lommel United . Both sides entered the pitch with clear ambitions, setting the stage for a match where every decision and clinical moment would carry immense weight. Valencia Ignites the Contest The opening exchanges were characterized by high energy, but it was Lommel United who found the clinical edge first. In the 31st minute, Anthony Valencia broke the deadlock with a sharp finish, silencing the home crowd and giving the visitors a vital 1-0 lead. The goal shifted the momentum, forcing Kortrijk to take more risks in their build-up play. As the first half progressed, the game became increasingly physical. Matthew Anderson received a yellow card in the 37th minute as the referee looked to keep control of a tightening contest. Despite several attempts from the hosts to find an immediate response, Lommel United maintained their composure to head into the break with their lead intact. A Brace and a Fightback The second half saw the visitors extend their dominance. In the 65th minute, Eran Tuypens turned provider, setting up Anthony Valencia for his second goal of the match. With the score at 2-0, Lommel United looked to be cruising toward a comfortable victory, prompting a flurry of tactical substitutions from both managers. However, Kortrijk refused to surrender. Following a series of changes, including the introduction of Bryan Adinany , the hosts found a lifeline. In the 80th minute, Xander Dierckx delivered a precise assist for Rein Van Helden , who clinicaly found the net to make it 2-1. The goal transformed the atmosphere, setting up a frantic final ten minutes. Defensive Grit in the Closing Stages The final whistle blew after three minutes of stoppage time, confirming a hard-fought victory for Lommel United . While Kortrijk pushed players forward in a desperate search for an equalizer, the visitors' defensive reinforcements, including Maxime Busi , held firm to secure the three points. It was a game of two halves for the hosts, but ultimately, Valencia 's individual brilliance proved to be the deciding factor."
